@startuml search
!include style.iuml
title Search: Query to Ranked Clips, and Learning from Shares

actor "Person" as U
participant "Test page\nindex.html" as PG
participant "API\napi.py" as A
participant "Search\nsearch.py" as S
participant "Embedder\nembed.py" as E
participant "Laya\nlaya-serve :8000" as L
participant "Indexer\nindexing.py" as I
database "Postgres\npgvector + pg_trgm" as DB

== QUERY ==
U -> PG : types "salary day"
PG -> A : GET /search?q=salary day
A -> S : search(conn, q, limit=24)
alt empty query
  S -> DB : TRENDING_SQL
  note right of S
    Most shared + most re-uploaded first.
  end note
end
S -> S : normalise(q)
note right of S
  **text.py · normalise()**
  Same function used at indexing time:
  Devanagari to Roman, lowercase, stretched
  letters collapsed, chat spellings unified.
  "salary day" -> "salary day"
end note
S -> E : embed_one("salary day")
E --> S : 384-number vector
S -> L : query_intent("salary day")
note right of L
  **laya.py · query_intent()**
  Two choice questions: topic (19 + none)
  and mood (13 + none). Keeps the top 2 of
  each at >= 0.3. Cached (2048 queries),
  3 s limit; any failure returns {} and
  search goes on without it.
end note
L --> S : money 0.99, happy 0.56

== RANK ==
S -> DB : SEARCH_SQL (qn, vector, tokens, intent)
note right of DB
  **candidates**
  fuzzy trigram match on s_* columns
  + 50 nearest embeddings
  + clips whose topics or reactions
    overlap the intent
end note
note right of DB
  **per candidate**
  kw  = best word_similarity over s_* columns
  sem = 1 - cosine distance
  tm  = sum of intent weights matching
        topics or reactions (max 1)
  score = 0.65 kw + 0.35 sem
        + 0.25 tm (1 - kw) + popularity
  shown if kw >= 0.35 or sem >= 0.45
        or tm >= 0.5
end note
DB --> S : clip 6: kw 0.21, sem 0.15, tm 0.99, score 0.385
S -> DB : INSERT INTO query_log
note right of DB
  Zero-result queries show up at
  GET /queries/failed: the list of
  missing clips or missing fields.
end note
S --> A : ranked rows
A --> PG : results + intent
PG --> U : cards, "read as money 0.99, happy 0.56"

== LEARN FROM A SHARE ==
U -> PG : clicks Share on clip 6
PG -> A : POST /clips/6/share {q: "salary day"}
A -> S : record_share(conn, 6, q)
S -> DB : shares + 1, learned_queries["salary day"] + 1
note right of S
  **search.py · record_share()**
  A query that ended in a share becomes a
  way to find the clip: real behaviour,
  not a model's guess. Next time
  "salary day" matches clip 6 by its words.
end note
S -> I : refresh(conn, 6, embed=False)
I -> DB : UPDATE s_learned
A --> PG : ok
PG --> U : link copied
@enduml
